tions are available: Apply the action to all drives  attached  to
the  controller.  Specify the control device to use.  The default
is Increased verbosity.  The following  commands  are  available:
Display  the  controller’s current status.  Display the status of
the specified drives.  This  command  returns  0  if  all  drives
tested  are online, 1 if one or more drives are critical and 2 if
one or more are offline.  Re‐scan the logical  drive  table,  and
attach  or  detach  devices from the system as necessary.  Detach
the specified drives.  Drives must be unmounted and unopened  for
this command to succeed.  Initiate a consistency check and repair
pass  on a drive that provides redundancy (e.g., RAID1 or RAID5).
This command returns immediately.  The command  can  be  used  to
monitor  the  progress  of the check.  Rebuild onto the specified
physical drive.  Note that there can be only one running  rebuild
operation per controller at any given time.  This command returns
immediately.   The command can be used to monitor the progress of
